sieve-filter-v2
; Letter triples: three letters may stand in a row inside a word only if some word of the
; list has them so, counting a word's start and end as a letter of their own (so "^ng" and
; "xq^" are triples too). A much stronger sieve than letter-pairs, still with no dictionary
; of whole words. The start of the unit may be the middle of a word, so its first letters are
; judged by pairs until there are three. States: 0 the start, 1 after a SPACE, then
; 2 + a * 26 + x for the last two, a being 0 unknown, 1 a word's start, 2 + n letter n.
; Generated by tools/build_text_plugins.py from scowl-2020.12.07-en-80-names.txt (sha256 d4aece883446c883591ad8c47ef265af945497fa4105aef6ccc30fd7dbfe2cba).
id        letter-triples
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     text
symbols   lower27
describe  No three letters in a row inside a word that no word of the list has in a row.
param     min_words  int  1  1  10  how many words of the list must have a pair or triple for it to be allowed

states    730
start     0
accept    0..729
